// The slots of wg_cur, the message wlgen is reading: its name (interface, an underscore and the message), its signature one letter per argument, the interface of its new_id argument ("" when it has none), and the prefix of the enum being read.
int wg_c_name = 0;
int wg_c_sig = 1;
int wg_c_new = 2;
int wg_c_pre = 3;

// The comment that opens the generated block. idstd/run.sh's wl section looks for its first line to find where the block starts.
string wg_head = "// BEGIN GENERATED by idc/tools/wlgen from the XML beside it (idc/tools/wlgen/*.xml) -- do not edit; idstd/run.sh's wl section regenerates this block and fails when it differs.\n// idstd_wl_ifn and idstd_wl_ifv: interface names and versions, indexed by interface number. idstd_wl_rs, idstd_wl_ri, idstd_wl_ro, idstd_wl_rn: for each request, by flat index, its signature, interface number, opcode and the number of the interface its new_id creates (-1 for none). idstd_wl_es, _ei, _eo, _en the same for events, and idstd_wl_eb the flat index of each interface's first event. idstd_wl_q_* and idstd_wl_e_* are those flat indexes by name; idstd_wl_n_* are enum entries.\n";
